.TH GIT-EZ 1 "" "git-ez" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-ez \- AI-assisted native Git integration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git ez
.RI "rebase|merge|cherry-pick target " [ options ]
.br
.B git ez
.RI "rebase|merge|cherry-pick --continue " [ options ]
.br
.B git ez
.RI "audit list|show " [ options ]
.br
.B git ez probe
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Git-ez delegates integration operations to native Git. When an eligible textual
conflict needs assistance, an agent investigates the repository and proposes
edits. Git-ez verifies the proposal, performs configured validation and controls
staging and native continuation.
.PP
Use
.B git-ez --help
or
.B git-ez COMMAND --help
for the complete option list supplied by the installed executable.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --repo " directory"
Select the repository. Filesystem symbolic links and parent components retain
native path semantics.
.TP
.B --interactive
Review the complete proposal before accepting it. Reject with feedback to request
a revision, or quit to restore the original tracked conflict state.
.TP
.BI --check " command arguments..."
Validate with literal command arguments. Place this option last; the remaining
arguments belong to the validation command.
.TP
.B --continue
Continue an existing native operation. Assistance eligibility follows the current
Git operation state; unrelated native failures remain manual recovery tasks.
.TP
.B --quiet, -q
Suppress git-ez progress and successful assisted summaries. Native Git output,
interactive review, errors and warnings remain visible.
.TP
.B --verbose, -v
Include model request, tool-name and reported-token metadata. Integration
verbosity options control git-ez only; the last one wins. They are not forwarded
to Git. Audit show retains its existing verbose evidence behavior.
.SH TERMINAL OUTPUT
Native Git stdout and stderr retain their routing. Native-only success adds no
git-ez summary. Progress, assisted summaries, reviews and recovery advice use
stderr. Help, version, audit results and probe JSON use stdout.
.PP
Capable stderr terminals receive elapsed-time spinners; pipes and dumb terminals
receive stage lines without animation. No colors are used, including when
NO_COLOR is set. Model tokens, reasoning and tool payloads are not streamed.
.PP
Review separates captured diffs and model-reported rationale from git-ez content
checks and user check results. Numerical model confidence remains in the audit.
Check output is captured; failure shows bounded excerpts and retained diagnostic
locations when available. A final check failure does not undo completed Git
integration and never recommends continuing an already completed operation.
.PP
The former Status/Git integration completed/Journal stdout block is replaced by
human summaries on stderr. Scripts parsing those strings must adapt; exit-code,
probe JSON and offline audit contracts are unchanged.
See docs/terminal.md for examples and statistics definitions.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Use native Git configuration under
.BR ez.* .
Set
.B ez.model
and configure the provider and endpoint as required. Supported protocols are
OpenAI-compatible and native Ollama. Consult the distributed
.B docs/configuration.md
for keys, defaults, credentials and TLS configuration.
.SH AUDIT
.B git ez audit list
lists saved AI interventions.
.B git ez audit show
inspects a saved run; use command help for verbose, artifact and session options.
Consultation is offline and does not require provider credentials.
Model-free operations do not create persistent LLM audit runs.
.SH SAFETY
Git remains responsible for operation state and recovery. Inspect the reported
failure and native Git status before continuing or aborting an interrupted
operation. Agent command controls do not constitute an operating-system sandbox.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Git 2.38 or later on a supported Linux, FreeBSD or macOS system.
A recent Git is recommended. Older Git may omit a Signed-off-by trailer when
continuing a conflicted rebase (fixed upstream in Git 2.46.0). Git-ez retains
this native behavior; cryptographic commit signatures are separate.
The standalone executable does not require Python or an installed manual.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-merge (1),
.BR git-rebase (1),
.BR git-cherry-pick (1)
